               <msContents>
                  <textLang mainLang="la">Latin</textLang>
                  <msItem>
                     <title>Ivo Carnotensis, Panormia; formula causarum sive iudiciorum</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">The formula is in a slightly later hand than
                        the rest, occupying fols 130--139. Vol. consists of 140 fols parchment 10"x
                        6" , in original boards and leather cover. No illumination, but capitals
                        finely executed in red and green. All information from Fr. A. Gwynn S.J. 35
                        Lower Leeson St., Dublin C.10 (9 March 1939).</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="11XX/12XX" notBefore="1100" notAfter="1299" calendar="#gregorian">s. xii/xiii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_219">Fountains, Yorkshire. Cistercian
                        abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>'C xi' (fol. 1r, red, same stayle
                        as capitals in text, s. xiii); 'Thecla .1a. in Antiq' Alm' lib' xxxviij'
                        (inside cover, facing first pressmark, later hand); 'Liber sancte Marie de
                        ffontibus' (s. xiii, fol. 4r).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Slingesby family (living near Fountains): Sir
                     Henry Slingesby 1647 (fol. 4r). Given 1699 to Dr. William Nicholson, archdeacon
                     (later bp.) of Carlisle by the bp's chaplain Galfrid' Wybergh. Nicholson died
                     as archbishop of Cashel 1726 and the book passed to the family of Daniel Hearn,
                     archdeacon of Cashel. Belonged to one Daniel Hearn 1816 whence it came to
                     Clongowes Jesuit College (founded 1814): date of accession
                     unrecorded.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Contemporary binding of thick wooden boards
                     covered with a leather jacket. The spine has projections at top and bottom. Two
                     clasps fastening on to lower cover now missing.</provenance>
               </history>
